1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:01:04,648 --> 00:01:07,484
<i>Sometimes, I get so caught up working</i>

3
00:01:07,568 --> 00:01:09,653
<i>and end up alone in the office.</i>

4
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:12,781
<i>When that happens</i>

5
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:15,284
<i>part of me wants to leave
as soon as I can</i>

6
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,579
<i>while another part of me</i>

7
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,664
<i>feels proud of working hard.</i>

8
00:01:22,124 --> 00:01:25,252
<i>I even fool myself into thinking</i>

9
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:27,004
<i>I'm the most important person
in the company.</i>

10
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:33,051
<i>I have 1.3 billion won.</i>

11
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:38,056
<i>But that's not enough to quit my job
or completely change my life.</i>

12
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:43,770
<i>I can't decide what to do
with the money.</i>

13
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,940
<i>So I continue going to work.</i>

14
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:58,744
<i>In the meantime,
while I'm stuck in indecision...</i>

15
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:04,499
<i>someone else is taking
the biggest leap of their life.</i>

16
00:02:30,359 --> 00:02:32,444
RESIGNATION LETTER
JEONG SEON-HYUK

17
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:37,324
If you want a raise or more benefits,
or if the work is too tough

18
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:40,410
just say so
instead of pulling a stunt like this.

19
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,623
It's not that.
I'm really planning to leave.

20
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:48,418
Isn't your kid starting school soon?
Can you afford to quit?

21
00:02:48,877 --> 00:02:51,338
Yes, we'll be fine for now.

22
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,300
What brought this on all of a sudden?

23
00:02:55,634 --> 00:02:58,261
Honestly, didn't you
see this coming, Ms. Park?

24
00:02:58,804 --> 00:03:00,055
If I try to make a move

25
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:03,016
it feels like I'm getting in the way
of the others' promotions.

26
00:03:03,642 --> 00:03:05,352
But if I do nothing

27
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:08,063
it feels like I'm holding back
the newer, younger employees.

28
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:11,983
Mr. Jeong, you are so...

29
00:03:12,067 --> 00:03:13,235
Pathetic, aren't I?

30
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:14,695
Trust me, I know.

31
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:16,405
I know that

32
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:19,741
but once I took a passive approach

33
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:22,077
it was hard to break out of it.

34
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:25,997
So I'm trying to change
my environment instead.

35
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:29,126
Starting your own business?

36
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:35,674
I won't make you sign
a non-compete agreement

37
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:37,175
so be honest with me.

38
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:55,068
EPISODE 4:
MUTUAL CAUSE, MUTUAL EFFECT

39
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,573
- Hello, Ju-hui.
- Hello.

40
00:04:00,866 --> 00:04:02,492
Come on, get to work on time.

41
00:04:02,576 --> 00:04:03,702
A team leader shouldn't be last.

42
00:04:04,453 --> 00:04:06,079
Right, my apologies.

43
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:08,039
You've been
exactly 13 minutes late lately.

44
00:04:08,123 --> 00:04:09,124
Going to the gym?

45
00:04:09,458 --> 00:04:11,084
I had something to take care of.

46
00:04:14,129 --> 00:04:15,422
We all have our own things going on.

47
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:19,176
That's an excuse for a rookie,
not a team leader.

48
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:22,262
I'm sorry.

49
00:04:27,851 --> 00:04:29,102
And where's Mr. Jeong?

50
00:04:30,145 --> 00:04:32,439
Even if he's quitting,
he should still get here on time.

51
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,399
Isn't that common courtesy?

52
00:04:34,483 --> 00:04:36,485
He said he was going
to stop by the mall today

53
00:04:36,568 --> 00:04:38,278
to say his goodbyes.

54
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:42,073
Everyone's just doing
whatever they want.

55
00:04:42,741 --> 00:04:44,659
Is this a playground?
A train station?

56
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:49,456
How ridiculous.

57
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,005
All right, let's start the meeting.

58
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:58,340
We have a lot to go over.

59
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:01,885
Gi-tae, when are you going
to the mall?

60
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,428
I'll head over right after lunch.

61
00:05:03,512 --> 00:05:05,514
They need to finish construction
this week

62
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:07,265
so keep morale up,
but keep the pressure on too.

63
00:05:07,349 --> 00:05:08,350
Got it.

64
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:10,769
Also, tonight at 8 p.m.

65
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,312
You remember, correct?

66
00:05:12,604 --> 00:05:13,605
Yes.

67
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,193
6TH FLOOR SALES DIVISION 1

68
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:26,076
Assistant Manager Jang Hyang-eun
will join our team next week.

69
00:05:27,077 --> 00:05:28,078
But she's already here.

70
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:29,496
Pardon?

71
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:31,873
Hello, Mr. Gong.

72
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:35,710
Oh, hello, Ms. Jang.

73
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,338
What brings you here?

74
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:41,383
I came to say hello
and meet our business partners.

75
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,093
Have you been well?

76
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:44,511
Yes, it's been a long time.

77
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:45,762
Right.

78
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:47,430
Hello, Mr. Yang.

79
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:50,183
Wow, long time no see.
I look forward to working with you.

80
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:52,060
Likewise.

81
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:54,312
You haven't met these two yet,
have you?

82
00:05:54,396 --> 00:05:56,231
- This is...
- Gi-tae?

83
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:57,440
Hello, ma'am.

84
00:05:57,983 --> 00:05:59,025
I've heard a lot about you.

85
00:05:59,568 --> 00:06:01,069
All good things, I hope.

86
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:02,779
Yes, of course.

87
00:06:03,947 --> 00:06:04,948
And you're Ji-hye?

88
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,992
I look forward
to working with you, ma'am.

89
00:06:07,242 --> 00:06:09,744
- Are you managing the center?
- Yes.

90
00:06:09,828 --> 00:06:11,329
Can I ask you a favor?

91
00:06:11,413 --> 00:06:12,873
Of course, anything.

92
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:15,333
I'd like the following information
by my first official day.

93
00:06:15,417 --> 00:06:18,044
Baseline margins for the brands
Team 5 is in charge of.

94
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:19,337
Customer prices.

95
00:06:19,421 --> 00:06:21,047
Each brand's customer service manual.

96
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:22,340
Credit memo logs.

97
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:23,592
Invoice checklists.

98
00:06:23,675 --> 00:06:25,260
Total penalty points.

99
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:28,054
Direct numbers for all brand reps
as well as their email addresses.

100
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:30,348
Can you put that together for me?

101
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:36,104
Baseline margins, customer prices...

102
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:37,564
Customer service manuals.

103
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:39,149
I'd be disappointed
if I had to repeat myself.

104
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:43,570
I'll say hello to Ms. Park.

105
00:06:49,284 --> 00:06:50,285
That's Ms. Jang.

106
00:06:51,244 --> 00:06:52,662
She was always good at her job, no?

107
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:54,289
She hasn't changed a bit.

108
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:55,832
Is this right?

109
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:57,375
Will Ji-hye and I be okay?

110
00:06:57,959 --> 00:06:59,419
Of course not.

111
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:00,795
You're screwed.

112
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:02,088
DAILY ROUTINE

113
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:03,256
<i>Thank you.</i>

114
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:09,638
I didn't know there was
a spot like this nearby.

115
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:11,473
Most of our colleagues don't know.

116
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:13,600
I stop by every morning before work.

117
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:17,020
So you called me to ask
about Jang Hyang-eun, right?

118
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:20,190
Yeah, she's joining my team,
so I need to know more about her.

119
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:22,150
I told you all I know last time.

120
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:24,277
Something happened
while she was at the China branch.

121
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:27,364
But they kept a tight lid on it,
so no one knows the details.

122
00:07:28,073 --> 00:07:31,701
They froze all personnel transfers,
but she managed to return to Korea.

123
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:33,370
That's everything.

124
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,580
So you don't actually know anything.

125
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:37,040
I don't.

126
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:39,751
But nothing good will come
from getting involved with her.

127
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,419
Whatever she did while she was there

128
00:07:41,503 --> 00:07:43,838
it'll only make it harder
to work with the China branch.

129
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:45,799
All right, then.

130
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:47,467
I'm sure she'll tell me
when she's ready.

131
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:50,637
That's a good mindset.
Just take it easy.

132
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:53,890
All you need to think about is
how to utilize your team members.

133
00:07:54,391 --> 00:07:56,309
Ms. Jang should take over
the center now.

134
00:07:57,811 --> 00:08:00,522
I said, think about it.
Really think it through.

135
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,819
What about Lee Ji-hye?

136
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:08,196
She's only a contract worker,
so she must be anxious already.

137
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:10,907
And now this woman flies in
from China and takes her spot?

138
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:12,534
How do you think she'd feel?

139
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:16,246
Even so, work is work.

140
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:20,041
You're so cold-blooded.

141
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:22,794
Don't you have any empathy?

142
00:08:24,713 --> 00:08:25,964
What about you?

143
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:28,341
You claim to be such an empath.

144
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:30,635
But why don't you empathize with me?

145
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:33,054
You sure have a way with words.

146
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:37,183
Anyway, keep doing your job

147
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:40,770
but don't forget to look out
for your team, Mr. Gong.

148
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:43,606
I got this for you.

149
00:08:44,107 --> 00:08:46,651
Try it. It'll bring out your empathy.

150
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:56,036
It's good.

151
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:57,203
See, I told you.

152
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:05,754
Hello, Mr. Yang.

153
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:09,090
I just arrived at the store.

154
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:10,967
Sure, I'll send you a photo.

155
00:09:11,051 --> 00:09:12,260
All right.

156
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:14,763
VITAMIN ENERGY DRINK

157
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:19,684
Okay.

158
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,608
Hello, sir.
Thank you for your hard work.

159
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,151
Hey, get off me.

160
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:29,527
I'm already hot as it is.

161
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:31,780
My goodness.

162
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:33,782
Construction is practically done.

163
00:09:33,865 --> 00:09:34,866
Done, my foot.

164
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,326
We've got a long way to go.

165
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,453
We worked until 2 a.m. last night.

166
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:41,456
Don't give us last-minute orders.

167
00:09:41,539 --> 00:09:43,249
You always cut it close.

168
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,628
Come on now.

169
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:49,172
Have a drink, sir.

170
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:50,256
- Fine.
- All right.

171
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:53,676
Have a drink while you work.

172
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:56,930
Here you go.
Thank you for your hard work.

173
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:01,893
Gosh, it's so dusty in here.

174
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:03,978
This just won't do.

175
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:07,398
Hi, is this General Affairs?

176
00:10:07,482 --> 00:10:09,192
I'm calling from the Laknes store.

177
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,902
Can you send someone to vacuum?

178
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:12,570
Sorry?

179
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:16,199
You should know
where the Laknes store is by now.

180
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:20,286
Do you have any idea
how hard these people are working?

181
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:23,289
Yes, please be more considerate.

182
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:25,750
Thank you in advance.

183
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:28,336
- Jeez.
- Goodness.

184
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:30,338
You Hongsung people, I swear...

185
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:33,258
So should we start
the electrical work?

186
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:34,968
You're the best.

187
00:10:35,552 --> 00:10:37,345
We're counting on you.

188
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:38,429
Whatever.

189
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:40,849
Let's start on electrical.

190
00:10:40,932 --> 00:10:42,058
We can follow the blueprint.

191
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,852
All right, let's see.

192
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:46,020
Since this is a clothing store...

193
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:49,107
- These aren't heavy at all.
- Just leave them. We'll handle it.

194
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,025
It's the least I can do.

195
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:52,485
Light as a feather.

196
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:16,926
- Hey, Gi-tae.
<i>- Hello, Mr. Yang.</i>

197
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,553
<i>Construction is going well.</i>

198
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:20,096
They're cleaning up now.

199
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,390
<i>Okay, good work.
Are you coming back now?</i>

200
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,893
Oh, since I'm here

201
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:27,478
I figured I'd make my rounds
at the other stores.

202
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:29,898
Good idea. But don't go empty-handed.

203
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:31,649
<i>Buy them something to drink.</i>

204
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:33,735
Understood, sir.

205
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:35,904
I'll see you later, then.

206
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:37,405
All right. Good work.

207
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:41,701
Gi-tae's gotten pretty savvy.

208
00:11:42,911 --> 00:11:45,205
- It looks too cramped, doesn't it?
- Yes.

209
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:47,165
It might fall off the edge.

210
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:50,710
How about this...

211
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:53,087
I think it's okay now.

212
00:11:58,218 --> 00:11:59,969
Over here, Mr. Jeong.

213
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:08,102
Were you checking on construction?

214
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:10,438
Yes.

215
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:20,865
Have a seat.

216
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:32,919
Did you make your rounds?

217
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:36,381
Yes, I said hello
to everyone at the office.

218
00:12:36,673 --> 00:12:38,299
How does it feel to be back?

219
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,261
It's great, of course.

220
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:43,263
A bit awkward too.

221
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:45,890
You must have a lot on your mind.

222
00:12:47,392 --> 00:12:49,269
I'm not entirely at ease.

223
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,772
It wasn't an easy decision
for me, either.

224
00:12:53,815 --> 00:12:56,526
I wasn't sure taking you in
was the right call.

225
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:01,197
I completely understand
where you're coming from.

226
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:02,615
Let me be clear.

227
00:13:03,074 --> 00:13:05,451
Just because I approved it
doesn't mean I was happy about it.

228
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:07,912
Yes, ma'am.

229
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:12,041
The audit of the China branch
is starting now.

230
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:15,169
Depending on the outcome,
it could turn into a criminal case.

231
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:16,296
Are you aware of that?

232
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,339
Yes, I'm aware.

233
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:20,174
I can't help but wonder.

234
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:22,885
All personnel transfers were frozen

235
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:25,930
but how did just one person
transfer to Korea?

236
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:27,473
On top of that

237
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:30,935
I heard a complaint
was filed against you.

238
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:35,523
Did you abandon a sinking ship
to save yourself?

239
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:43,239
I don't know
if you can't say anything

240
00:13:43,323 --> 00:13:45,658
or if you're just choosing
to stay silent.

241
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,370
But I think it's possible

242
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:52,874
you're in league with the people
who embezzled from the China branch.

243
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:53,958
But...

244
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:57,211
We shouldn't assume anything
without evidence.

245
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,922
That's why I took you in.

246
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:02,550
Yes, ma'am.

247
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:05,678
There's only one thing
you can do here.

248
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,390
Work hard.

249
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:14,354
If the audit results are positive,
that's great news for you.

250
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:16,564
And even if they're negative

251
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:20,276
your hard work will still count
for something.

252
00:14:20,902 --> 00:14:22,362
Do you get what I'm saying?

253
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:24,030
Yes, ma'am.

254
00:14:24,697 --> 00:14:26,491
All right, you may go.

255
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:29,786
Yes, ma'am.

256
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:07,740
2 MONTHS AGO, CHINA

257
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:10,660
POINT OF CONTACT

258
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,245
TRADING COMPANY TRANSACTIONS

259
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:27,427
COPY TO USB DRIVE

260
00:15:29,512 --> 00:15:30,638
Who's there?

261
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,571
CUSTOMER SERVICE MANUAL

262
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:47,780
What are you working on?

263
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:51,826
The documents Ms. Jang requested.

264
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:53,995
Are you putting them together
like this?

265
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:57,206
Is this not good enough?

266
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,626
No, you're doing great.

267
00:16:00,918 --> 00:16:02,086
- Mr. Yang.
- Yes?

268
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:05,923
Mr. Gong, it's time for lunch.

269
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,675
Is it?

270
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:09,218
Let's go.

271
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:10,845
Come on, Ji-hye.

272
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:13,014
I'm not really hungry.

273
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:14,307
You two go ahead.

274
00:16:14,724 --> 00:16:16,893
How can you work on an empty stomach?

275
00:16:17,268 --> 00:16:18,769
Should I get you
a salad or something?

276
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:20,438
No, I'll be fine.

277
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:21,731
Enjoy your lunch.

278
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:28,779
Mr. Jeong hasn't come in yet?

279
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:31,032
No, and he's not answering his phone.

280
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,311
- Hello.
- Hello.

281
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:01,854
- Hello.
- Yes, hello.

282
00:17:01,938 --> 00:17:04,315
- Hello.
- Good day.

283
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:08,611
CEO'S OFFICE

284
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:16,744
CEO JEONG SEON-HYUK

285
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:19,872
Yes?

286
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:22,500
Would you like some coffee, sir?

287
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,210
That would be lovely.

288
00:17:35,096 --> 00:17:38,057
MANTUA, ITALY

289
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:50,278
Mr. Jeong.

290
00:17:50,361 --> 00:17:51,696
<i>Hi, Mr. Sponza.</i>

291
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:53,531
<i>I just got your invoice.</i>

292
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:54,991
All is good. See?

293
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:57,326
I'll send everything out like that.

294
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:58,786
Thank you.

295
00:18:01,122 --> 00:18:03,666
Did you get any call from Hongsung?

296
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:04,750
<i>No.</i>

297
00:18:04,959 --> 00:18:07,378
But even if they did,
don't worry.

298
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:08,838
<i>Okay.</i>

299
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,464
<i>I'll call you again soon.</i>

300
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:11,549
Okay.

301
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:23,644
I'll do everything I can
to set the mood.

302
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:25,688
- No, don't do anything.
- Yes, sir.

303
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:27,773
I'll handle Ms. Cha.

304
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:28,899
Don't worry.

305
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:32,278
She may seem easy to sway,
but she doesn't open up easily.

306
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:34,488
I'll lighten the mood somehow.

307
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:35,906
I'll do my best to back you up.

308
00:18:36,157 --> 00:18:37,867
- Don't. Just stay put.
- Yes, sir. I'll stay put.

309
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:40,786
Let's give it our all today

310
00:18:40,870 --> 00:18:43,122
and get the best managers
on our side.

311
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:47,877
ANTACID

312
00:18:55,426 --> 00:18:56,469
You're having one too?

313
00:18:57,386 --> 00:18:58,554
Because we're a team.

314
00:19:48,104 --> 00:19:49,689
- Here they come.
- What?

315
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,359
- Don't be nervous.
- Yes, sir.

316
00:19:54,402 --> 00:19:55,736
- Hey.
- Hello, ladies!

317
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:57,196
Let me take that for you.

318
00:19:57,279 --> 00:20:00,032
We've been waiting forever
for you ladies.

319
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:01,617
- Right this way.
- Hello.

320
00:20:01,951 --> 00:20:02,952
Hello.

321
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:04,954
- Have a seat right here.
- Hello.

322
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:08,165
When is Hongsung going to hire
some new people?

323
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:10,209
It's always the same faces.

324
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:12,002
All old and worn-out.

325
00:20:12,086 --> 00:20:13,421
That's harsh, Ms. Cha.

326
00:20:13,504 --> 00:20:14,880
I'm still in my twenties.

327
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:16,674
No, you're definitely not.

328
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:18,592
I swear I am.

329
00:20:18,676 --> 00:20:20,052
No, I don't believe you.

330
00:20:20,136 --> 00:20:22,012
- Just pour us some drinks.
- Thank you.

331
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:24,265
All right, give me your glasses.

332
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:48,873
Delicious, isn't it?

333
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:59,175
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

334
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,761
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

335
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:04,597
Laknes?

336
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:07,683
Didn't they go out of business?

337
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:09,518
You've got it all wrong.

338
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:13,189
They strategically decided to wait
for the market to peak.

339
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:14,774
That's called going out of business.

340
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,358
It's true. They did.

341
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,861
But market trends
are always changing.

342
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:21,113
Now is the right time
for Laknes to make a comeback.

343
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:23,991
Exactly.

344
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:26,076
Fine, let's say
they went out of business.

345
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:28,037
They already failed once.

346
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,247
Would they try again without a plan?

347
00:21:30,331 --> 00:21:33,584
They prepared thoroughly
for their comeback.

348
00:21:34,168 --> 00:21:37,087
Being prepared is great and all

349
00:21:37,171 --> 00:21:39,381
but Ms. Cha recently...

350
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:42,760
Can I tell them?

351
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:44,762
Of course not.

352
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,388
- I shouldn't.
- What is it?

353
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,140
So the thing is

354
00:21:48,599 --> 00:21:49,934
she got an offer from a certain brand

355
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:53,145
to run their flagship store
in Seongsu-dong.

356
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:55,856
Habsburg?

357
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:58,359
How did you...

358
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:00,694
Of course, I know everything
that happens in this industry.

359
00:22:01,779 --> 00:22:02,947
But that place is...

360
00:22:03,572 --> 00:22:04,990
Sure, it's nice.

361
00:22:05,074 --> 00:22:06,826
We can't stop you from going there.

362
00:22:07,368 --> 00:22:10,746
Don't they offer managers
a 15% commission?

363
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,957
I'm sure that's true
for the first month.

364
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,543
But they'll lower it
after their opening month.

365
00:22:15,626 --> 00:22:16,669
I already know.

366
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:19,171
How do you know?

367
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:22,967
Those punks always
pull the same scheme.

368
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:24,051
Ms. Cha.

369
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:26,136
I wasn't going to say this, but...

370
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:31,183
Sis.

371
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:33,394
You're really breaking my heart.

372
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:34,770
What?

373
00:22:35,855 --> 00:22:37,064
Why are you so naive?

374
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:40,317
You've been played so many times,
but you still don't get it.

375
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:42,319
This isn't the first time
they've pulled this.

376
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:45,531
Why do you keep working with them
when they play you every time?

377
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:48,033
Why do you always turn us down

378
00:22:48,117 --> 00:22:50,661
and choose to suffer
working with those punks?

379
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:54,164
I swear I'm not saying this
because you won't work with us.

380
00:22:54,832 --> 00:22:57,251
How many years
have we known each other?

381
00:22:57,334 --> 00:23:00,379
It just breaks my heart
to see you go through that!

382
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:02,423
Maybe you should stop drinking,
Mr. Yang.

383
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:05,384
Imagine she were your sister!

384
00:23:06,886 --> 00:23:07,887
Sis.

385
00:23:08,554 --> 00:23:09,638
Just promise me one thing.

386
00:23:11,015 --> 00:23:13,183
I can't force you to work with us

387
00:23:13,601 --> 00:23:16,437
but just don't let them hurt you.

388
00:23:16,854 --> 00:23:19,023
Give it your best shot.

389
00:23:19,690 --> 00:23:21,025
That's all I ask.

390
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:27,323
Damn, you almost got me.

391
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:29,450
That was so close.

392
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:30,910
I thought you were actually drunk.

393
00:23:30,993 --> 00:23:32,953
- We've got a long way to go.
- Oh, my gosh.

394
00:23:33,037 --> 00:23:34,413
- The night is young.
- Jeez.

395
00:23:34,997 --> 00:23:36,373
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

396
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,710
<i>She's so smart</i>

397
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,503
<i>She's so charming</i>

398
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:44,048
<i>She drives me crazy
I like her so much...</i>

399
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:45,591
Goodness.

400
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:47,092
Your glass is empty.

401
00:23:47,176 --> 00:23:48,636
Let me pour you a drink.

402
00:23:49,553 --> 00:23:52,973
I keep drinking,
but I wonder if it's poisoned.

403
00:23:53,057 --> 00:23:55,267
No poison, just sincerity.

404
00:23:55,351 --> 00:23:56,477
Pour me one too.

405
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:59,271
I can't deal with you, Mr. Yang.

406
00:23:59,355 --> 00:24:00,731
That's too bad. Deal with it.

407
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:05,027
When we get the Laknes samples,
I'll save you a horsehair bag.

408
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:08,030
If you're giving me one,
make it alligator.

409
00:24:08,739 --> 00:24:11,116
Alligator is nice too

410
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,118
but you haven't seen
their burgundy horsehair.

411
00:24:13,202 --> 00:24:14,370
It's beautiful.

412
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:16,080
Horsehair or alligator,
it doesn't matter.

413
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:17,790
The timing couldn't be worse.

414
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,124
Why did it have to be now?

415
00:24:23,045 --> 00:24:24,088
Do you think it'll work?

416
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:28,008
I don't know.

417
00:24:28,384 --> 00:24:31,595
Goodness, how can you say that
when you came here to convince me?

418
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:34,848
I'll be honest with you, Ms. Cha.

419
00:24:34,932 --> 00:24:36,475
I'm not sure about Laknes.

420
00:24:36,725 --> 00:24:39,603
But with you,
I think we can make it work.

421
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:42,147
Well, aren't you a smooth talker?

422
00:24:42,523 --> 00:24:44,149
Even if it's the same brand

423
00:24:44,233 --> 00:24:47,695
there can be a huge gap in revenue
depending on the manager.

424
00:24:47,778 --> 00:24:48,946
You know that yourself.

425
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:52,116
I wouldn't ask you
if I didn't believe in this brand.

426
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:54,743
If anyone could sell it,
then I'd ask anyone.

427
00:24:55,661 --> 00:24:57,830
But this is something
only you can do.

428
00:24:58,747 --> 00:25:01,458
Is that a good thing or a bad thing?

429
00:25:01,542 --> 00:25:03,335
As for incentives and benefits

430
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:05,713
I'll match the highest
industry standards.

431
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,007
Let's give it a shot, Ms. Cha.

432
00:25:10,092 --> 00:25:11,552
I'm getting played again.

433
00:25:12,302 --> 00:25:13,345
Come on.

434
00:25:13,429 --> 00:25:14,722
Have a drink.

435
00:25:15,848 --> 00:25:16,849
Drink up.

436
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:25,399
<i>I know you really need me</i>

437
00:25:25,482 --> 00:25:27,401
<i>- You're too perfect
- You're too perfect</i>

438
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:28,694
<i>- I saw your eyes...
- I saw your eyes...</i>

439
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:31,739
SINCHON <i>SEOLLEONGTANG</i>

440
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:42,875
Jeez, those chicks can really drink.

441
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,878
Why say that
after you had such a good time?

442
00:25:46,712 --> 00:25:47,713
Sorry?

443
00:25:49,506 --> 00:25:50,841
It's not right

444
00:25:50,924 --> 00:25:53,385
to bad-mouth people
after having a good time with them.

445
00:25:53,469 --> 00:25:55,262
We're the ones who need them.

446
00:25:56,138 --> 00:25:57,222
Well...

447
00:25:57,306 --> 00:25:59,641
I wasn't exactly bad-mouthing them.

448
00:25:59,725 --> 00:26:03,062
It was more like
an expression of surprise.

449
00:26:03,145 --> 00:26:05,647
Then just say
they can really hold their liquor.

450
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:08,067
Why are you calling them chicks
and saying they drink too much?

451
00:26:09,485 --> 00:26:11,862
You've been sprouting up lately.

452
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:13,155
Should I nip that in the bud?

453
00:26:14,448 --> 00:26:15,491
I'm sorry, sir.

454
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,036
- Mr. Yang.
- Thank you.

455
00:26:21,371 --> 00:26:22,956
- Gi-tae.
- Yes, sir.

456
00:26:23,916 --> 00:26:25,250
It's not just you, Gi-tae.

457
00:26:25,334 --> 00:26:26,376
That's human nature.

458
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:28,462
Everyone's different
behind closed doors.

459
00:26:28,879 --> 00:26:30,130
It's best to be careful.

460
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,008
Yes, sir. I'll keep that in mind.

461
00:26:34,927 --> 00:26:37,721
Don't forget what I said,
even if you go to a new company.

462
00:26:38,555 --> 00:26:39,556
Yes, sir.

463
00:26:40,891 --> 00:26:41,892
Sorry?

464
00:26:42,309 --> 00:26:45,020
So have you made a decision?

465
00:26:45,104 --> 00:26:46,271
Are you leaving the company?

466
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:47,731
What?

467
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:49,108
Are you quitting, Park Gi-tae?

468
00:26:50,192 --> 00:26:51,902
What? I mean...

469
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:53,779
What's with that guilty look?

470
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:55,114
You did nothing wrong.

471
00:26:55,197 --> 00:26:56,573
I'm just curious.

472
00:26:56,657 --> 00:27:00,077
<i>The luck that passed me by
came together...</i>

473
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,995
- Gi-tae, increase the echo.
- Okay.

474
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:08,001
<i>It became you and came to me</i>

475
00:27:08,085 --> 00:27:12,089
<i>In a rainstorm</i>

476
00:27:12,381 --> 00:27:13,423
<i>I'll become...</i>

477
00:27:13,507 --> 00:27:15,717
Thank you for the offer, Mr. Gong.

478
00:27:16,218 --> 00:27:17,970
Thank you for seeing me.

479
00:27:18,053 --> 00:27:20,597
But why did you come yourself
this time?

480
00:27:20,681 --> 00:27:22,933
Mr. Yang was always the one
who went drinking with us.

481
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:26,145
I thought you weren't on good terms
with your team.

482
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:28,355
I can't say that's entirely false.

483
00:27:28,939 --> 00:27:29,940
Are things better now?

484
00:27:30,566 --> 00:27:33,652
<i>...I'll go anywhere</i>

485
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:35,737
<i>Trust in me now...</i>

486
00:27:35,821 --> 00:27:38,115
Yes, I'm working on it.

487
00:27:40,742 --> 00:27:43,787
You should work a little harder.

488
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:45,998
Pardon?

489
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:52,254
<i>You know Mr. Jeong
started his own business.</i>

490
00:27:54,006 --> 00:27:56,425
<i>Did you know
he's been trying to scout people?</i>

491
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,468
He's much more friendly now.

492
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,220
Really? Mr. Gong?

493
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:01,471
- Yes.
- No way.

494
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:07,811
<i>Trust in me now</i>

495
00:28:10,272 --> 00:28:12,149
- Let's go, Laknes!
- Let's go!

496
00:28:13,025 --> 00:28:15,402
I wasn't trying to hide it from you.

497
00:28:15,861 --> 00:28:18,488
But I did get an offer
from Mr. Jeong.

498
00:28:19,031 --> 00:28:22,451
Hey, you should've told us
right away.

499
00:28:23,285 --> 00:28:24,286
I'm sorry, it's just...

500
00:28:24,995 --> 00:28:27,581
I didn't know how to bring it up.

501
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:28,665
So the thing is...

502
00:28:29,791 --> 00:28:31,043
How do I say this?

503
00:28:31,293 --> 00:28:32,711
I'm not the only one

504
00:28:33,879 --> 00:28:35,964
Mr. Jeong made an offer to.

505
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:39,218
What are you saying?

506
00:28:40,636 --> 00:28:45,933
He made offers to employees
on other teams as well.

507
00:28:46,433 --> 00:28:47,726
That seemed a bit problematic.

508
00:28:48,227 --> 00:28:50,479
So I was trying to think
of a way to tell you.

509
00:28:52,356 --> 00:28:53,482
As far as I know...

510
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,318
It's more than four people.

511
00:28:58,987 --> 00:29:02,032
What exactly is he trying to do?

512
00:29:05,327 --> 00:29:06,703
<i>What did Ms. Park say?</i>

513
00:29:07,204 --> 00:29:08,664
What do you think?

514
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:10,791
I said I was quitting,
and she said okay.

515
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,044
Maybe she thought it was inevitable.

516
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:15,712
She might've even felt grateful.

517
00:29:16,213 --> 00:29:17,214
Hey.

518
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:18,757
I have to move aside

519
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,968
so people like you
can move up the ladder.

520
00:29:23,637 --> 00:29:26,056
If you resign, where will you go?

521
00:29:29,184 --> 00:29:31,728
You're going to quit at 40
without a plan?

522
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:33,939
Does your wife know?

523
00:29:34,022 --> 00:29:35,524
Of course, she does.

524
00:29:35,607 --> 00:29:36,858
She told me to do whatever I want.

525
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:39,569
But she said she'd kill me
if I can't support the family.

526
00:29:47,661 --> 00:29:48,829
Don't you have regrets?

527
00:29:49,204 --> 00:29:50,372
Yes, I do.

528
00:29:51,999 --> 00:29:54,209
Sometimes, I wonder
if I should've worked harder.

529
00:29:54,293 --> 00:29:55,419
If I had

530
00:29:56,128 --> 00:29:58,255
could I have been
a candidate for associate director?

531
00:29:58,338 --> 00:29:59,339
That sort of thing.

532
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:01,049
Mr. Jeong.

533
00:30:02,259 --> 00:30:04,594
If you just get through
this promotion cycle

534
00:30:04,678 --> 00:30:06,096
I think you'll have a shot.

535
00:30:07,097 --> 00:30:08,098
Hey.

536
00:30:08,515 --> 00:30:10,225
You're skilled

537
00:30:10,309 --> 00:30:13,061
and gaining good work experience,
so you might not know this.

538
00:30:13,437 --> 00:30:15,897
But I wasn't promoted to team leader
based on my skills.

539
00:30:15,981 --> 00:30:17,149
It was based on seniority.

540
00:30:18,275 --> 00:30:21,486
Do you know the highest position
you can reach through seniority?

541
00:30:22,612 --> 00:30:23,905
Team leader.

542
00:30:23,989 --> 00:30:25,115
I'm a team leader.

543
00:30:25,490 --> 00:30:26,491
It's over for me.

544
00:30:29,036 --> 00:30:30,912
Aren't you thinking too negatively?

545
00:30:30,996 --> 00:30:32,622
You're the best at this job.

546
00:30:32,706 --> 00:30:33,915
What are you talking about?

547
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:35,917
Thanks for saying that.

548
00:30:36,001 --> 00:30:37,002
Jeez.

549
00:30:41,381 --> 00:30:42,382
Eun-tae.

550
00:30:43,216 --> 00:30:44,259
Someday

551
00:30:45,135 --> 00:30:48,221
if we ever meet again through work

552
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:51,058
I hope you won't be
too disappointed in me.

553
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:53,643
What are you saying?

554
00:30:53,727 --> 00:30:54,895
I'm just saying.

555
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:56,521
I hope you don't feel that way.

556
00:31:15,290 --> 00:31:17,334
INCOMING CALL
TEAM 4 MR. JEONG SEON-HYUK

557
00:31:20,921 --> 00:31:24,299
ASSISTANT MANAGER GONG EUN-TAE

558
00:31:24,383 --> 00:31:25,759
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hey, Eun-tae.

559
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:27,094
Did you eat dinner?

560
00:31:27,511 --> 00:31:28,845
<i>Why are you doing this?</i>

561
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:31,181
What are you referring to?

562
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:33,975
Not showing up to work
after resigning

563
00:31:34,226 --> 00:31:36,019
<i>or poaching employees?</i>

564
00:31:36,436 --> 00:31:37,437
Both, I suppose.

565
00:31:40,190 --> 00:31:42,025
<i>Well, once I thought about it</i>

566
00:31:42,526 --> 00:31:44,611
I realized I couldn't fake a smile
and say goodbye

567
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:46,822
when I'm betraying everyone.

568
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:49,241
That's why I haven't been to work.

569
00:31:49,908 --> 00:31:51,785
And it's true that I made job offers.

570
00:31:52,285 --> 00:31:53,829
<i>They can make their own decisions.</i>

571
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:56,498
So did you just call me
to ask if I had dinner?

572
00:31:58,834 --> 00:32:01,128
So what is Hongsung going to do?

573
00:32:02,629 --> 00:32:04,631
They'll have to punish me somehow.

574
00:32:05,882 --> 00:32:07,426
What exactly are you expecting?

575
00:32:08,135 --> 00:32:10,220
I'm sure you're not far off.

576
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:12,055
Is that right?

577
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:14,349
What about you?

578
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:16,184
Will you stay at Hongsung?

579
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:22,774
- What do you mean?
<i>- Do you know</i>

580
00:32:23,483 --> 00:32:25,902
what they all say
when I offer them a job?

581
00:32:26,695 --> 00:32:28,613
They thank me
for recognizing their worth.

582
00:32:29,197 --> 00:32:31,616
Hongsung doesn't know
how to develop its employees.

583
00:32:31,992 --> 00:32:33,910
<i>I mean, they have a guy like you</i>

584
00:32:33,994 --> 00:32:36,621
<i>caught up in office politics
and doing odd jobs.</i>

585
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:40,125
So why don't you take this chance
to think about it?

586
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:43,587
<i>I'll pretend we never had
this conversation.</i>

587
00:32:47,257 --> 00:32:49,468
HONGSUNG SALES DIVISION 1
TEAM LEADER JEONG SEON-HYUK

588
00:32:49,551 --> 00:32:50,552
Eun-tae.

589
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:53,513
You're the reason I'm leaving.

590
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:56,141
<i>I made this decision because of you.</i>

591
00:32:59,769 --> 00:33:05,025
<i>All I did was find the courage
to do the job I'd been given.</i>

592
00:33:06,359 --> 00:33:11,490
<i>I had no idea that courage
would lead to this result.</i>

593
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:13,074
You see...

594
00:33:14,451 --> 00:33:15,702
I think...

595
00:33:18,455 --> 00:33:20,165
I'll become Hongsung's enemy.

596
00:33:21,583 --> 00:33:24,294
<i>You could say the one
who made him Hongsung's enemy...</i>

597
00:33:26,463 --> 00:33:27,797
<i>was me.</i>

598
00:33:37,516 --> 00:33:39,267
- Good morning.
- Hello, Mr. Gong.

599
00:33:40,101 --> 00:33:41,937
- Hello.
- Hello.

600
00:33:42,604 --> 00:33:44,439
- Hello.
- Hello, sir.

601
00:33:44,940 --> 00:33:46,024
Hello.

602
00:33:46,107 --> 00:33:48,527
- You're here early, Ms. Jang.
- Hello, Mr. Gong.

603
00:33:48,610 --> 00:33:50,111
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

604
00:34:00,288 --> 00:34:03,041
What's going on between you two?

605
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:04,459
Look at this.

606
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:09,422
Didn't she do a great job?

607
00:34:09,506 --> 00:34:11,299
Ji-hye worked very hard on it.

608
00:34:11,925 --> 00:34:14,261
You didn't stay up all night
for this, did you?

609
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:16,763
Please tell me you didn't.

610
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:19,391
I'm sorry, Ms. Jang.

611
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:23,228
Tell me if anything is missing
or needs to be revised.

612
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:24,688
I'll fix it right away.

613
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:26,982
What I'm trying to say is...

614
00:34:32,112 --> 00:34:33,363
Ji-hye.

615
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,782
Do you have the original file?

616
00:34:36,116 --> 00:34:39,035
Yes, I shared it
on the company network.

617
00:34:39,411 --> 00:34:40,495
That's great.

618
00:34:40,579 --> 00:34:43,039
Let's use it as our team's manual.

619
00:34:43,915 --> 00:34:44,916
Sorry?

620
00:34:46,084 --> 00:34:47,627
I'm really sorry, Ji-hye.

621
00:34:47,711 --> 00:34:49,254
I should have been clearer.

622
00:34:50,171 --> 00:34:53,008
I was just asking
for a simple document

623
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:55,176
so I could begin working right away.

624
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:57,387
I wasn't asking you
to write a full report.

625
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:00,140
It's not like I'm a director.

626
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:02,183
I mean, this is flawless.

627
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:05,020
Even I can't make
something like this.

628
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:12,110
I was going to tell her,
but she was doing such a good job.

629
00:35:12,193 --> 00:35:13,778
I wanted to see the final result...

630
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:17,699
Ji-hye?

631
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:22,871
I'm sorry.

632
00:35:24,164 --> 00:35:25,999
I don't know what's wrong with me.

633
00:35:29,085 --> 00:35:30,337
I'm sorry.

634
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:38,428
I bet you've never been up here.

635
00:35:39,054 --> 00:35:40,096
No, I haven't.

636
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:43,600
I didn't even know
we had a place like this.

637
00:35:45,727 --> 00:35:46,728
I'm sorry.

638
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:49,481
I'm sorry
I didn't bring you here sooner

639
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:51,858
especially after you've been here
for over four months.

640
00:35:52,942 --> 00:35:56,321
And as your team leader,
I didn't know how anxious you were.

641
00:35:56,404 --> 00:35:57,614
I'm also sorry for that.

642
00:35:58,365 --> 00:36:01,826
I loved seeing how hard you worked,
so I left you alone.

643
00:36:02,911 --> 00:36:04,496
I had no clue it was out of anxiety.

644
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:09,709
You're a contract worker
who has just one year

645
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:11,920
to prove yourself
if you want to stay here.

646
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:13,254
It must be tough.

647
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:16,424
Well, I'm not the only one
in that position.

648
00:36:17,717 --> 00:36:19,260
I can do a better job.

649
00:36:20,679 --> 00:36:22,138
What exactly can you do better,
and how?

650
00:36:23,390 --> 00:36:24,391
I'll be honest.

651
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:27,143
I can't tell you

652
00:36:28,645 --> 00:36:31,314
to trust me and follow my lead,
or that hard work is all you need.

653
00:36:32,732 --> 00:36:33,858
But instead

654
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:36,528
I'll do everything I can
to deliver results

655
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:38,613
starting with Laknes.

656
00:36:39,489 --> 00:36:42,117
If the team gets good results,
I'll gain leverage as team leader.

657
00:36:42,492 --> 00:36:45,161
Then I'll have the confidence
to advocate for you

658
00:36:45,245 --> 00:36:50,375
because Sales Team 5 needs you,
no matter what.

659
00:37:01,261 --> 00:37:02,595
What is this?

660
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:04,764
It's the file you worked on.

661
00:37:05,432 --> 00:37:06,433
Keep it in your wallet.

662
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:08,893
Regardless of the outcome

663
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:13,773
it doesn't change your worth
as the person who made this.

664
00:37:15,191 --> 00:37:16,985
Don't put your faith in the company.

665
00:37:17,694 --> 00:37:19,028
Don't put your faith in me, either.

666
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:22,574
Trust in your own worth
as the creator of that file.

667
00:37:27,328 --> 00:37:29,330
Thank you, Mr. Gong.

668
00:37:32,959 --> 00:37:34,210
Stay up here a little longer.

669
00:37:34,753 --> 00:37:36,296
Just don't stay here all day.

670
00:37:40,633 --> 00:37:41,634
Mr. Gong.

671
00:37:42,844 --> 00:37:46,681
If I become a full-time employee,
I'll treat you to a meal.

672
00:37:48,057 --> 00:37:49,058
No.

673
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:51,686
I'll treat you.

674
00:37:52,604 --> 00:37:54,564
I promise I'll buy you
something delicious!

675
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:56,274
Make it premium Korean beef.

676
00:37:58,276 --> 00:37:59,277
All right.

677
00:38:18,546 --> 00:38:20,006
I'm sorry, Mr. Gong.

678
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:21,424
I should've made
my instructions clearer.

679
00:38:22,634 --> 00:38:24,844
It was ultimately my mistake.

680
00:38:24,928 --> 00:38:26,012
Don't worry about it.

681
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:31,392
Mr. Gong.

682
00:38:32,477 --> 00:38:34,604
I'm sure you have
many questions for me.

683
00:38:35,647 --> 00:38:36,981
Why haven't you asked me anything?

684
00:38:39,108 --> 00:38:40,944
If you had something to tell me,
you would've already.

685
00:38:42,028 --> 00:38:45,114
The fact that you haven't
means you're not ready yet.

686
00:38:47,784 --> 00:38:49,786
It wasn't an easy decision for me.

687
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:53,748
Please just know that.

688
00:39:03,925 --> 00:39:05,260
<i>How many people in total?</i>

689
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:07,762
Five, as far as we can tell.

690
00:39:07,846 --> 00:39:09,556
Team 1's Park Jin-u,
Team 2's Choi Ju-hui

691
00:39:09,639 --> 00:39:12,517
Team 3's Kang Yeong-seo,
Team 5's Park Gi-tae

692
00:39:13,226 --> 00:39:14,853
and Team 4's Oh Jeong-hyeon.

693
00:39:16,896 --> 00:39:18,648
He tried to completely
dismantle Team 4.

694
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,651
- Mr. Oh.
- Yes, ma'am.

695
00:39:21,734 --> 00:39:22,861
I rejected him right away.

696
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:25,363
Mr. Jeong didn't clock in
today, either?

697
00:39:26,239 --> 00:39:28,032
He also stopped taking our calls
since yesterday.

698
00:39:28,116 --> 00:39:29,117
I did some digging.

699
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:32,287
He appears to be mainly importing
gray market products from Mantua.

700
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:35,874
It seems he established contacts
in Mantua before he quit.

701
00:39:36,416 --> 00:39:39,377
He's also already taken
Safilo and Philipp Plein...

702
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:43,381
Were you aware?

703
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:46,384
Their sales figures were poor.

704
00:39:47,135 --> 00:39:49,554
It's been a while since they were
mentioned at the meetings.

705
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:54,309
Why didn't you stop him?

706
00:39:55,351 --> 00:39:56,978
I figured I'd let him have that much.

707
00:39:57,645 --> 00:39:59,772
I couldn't promote him, anyway.

708
00:40:00,315 --> 00:40:02,066
And he needed to find his own path.

709
00:40:03,610 --> 00:40:05,528
But poaching our people is
taking it too far.

710
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:09,824
- I think...
- Mr. Jang.

711
00:40:09,908 --> 00:40:10,909
Yes, ma'am.

712
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:12,660
What are your thoughts?

713
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:24,213
MULTI-BRAND SHOE STORE
PROJECT PROPOSAL

714
00:40:25,089 --> 00:40:26,174
What is this?

715
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:28,134
A project proposal
for a multi-brand shoe store?

716
00:40:28,217 --> 00:40:32,013
What if we used this
to put some pressure on Mr. Jeong?

717
00:40:38,895 --> 00:40:39,896
Tell me.

718
00:40:41,314 --> 00:40:42,398
Do you want to take this on?

719
00:40:42,815 --> 00:40:44,025
I'd like the company to take it on.

720
00:40:44,692 --> 00:40:46,527
If you propose this
as associate director

721
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:48,279
it won't just be Team 5's project.

722
00:40:48,363 --> 00:40:50,531
It'll become the entire
Sales Division's project.

723
00:40:59,374 --> 00:41:01,751
We have to break into this market
at some point, anyway.

724
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:05,797
Even if we sue Mr. Jeong,
we won't gain anything.

725
00:41:06,172 --> 00:41:08,466
And filing a claim against
our Mantua partners will be useless.

726
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:10,551
"We had no idea.
What do you expect us to do?"

727
00:41:10,635 --> 00:41:11,844
They'll feign ignorance.

728
00:41:12,595 --> 00:41:13,721
And, to be frank...

729
00:41:16,516 --> 00:41:19,227
we can't stop our employees
from wanting to leave.

730
00:41:19,978 --> 00:41:21,521
So I propose

731
00:41:21,771 --> 00:41:24,148
that we take all of Mantua back.

732
00:41:24,774 --> 00:41:28,486
You want to use the shoe supply
to put pressure on Mantua?

733
00:41:29,237 --> 00:41:31,698
Mr. Jeong gets his entire supply
from Mantua.

734
00:41:32,323 --> 00:41:36,494
So I suggest we become a client
Mantua can't afford to lose.

735
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:38,079
So big that Mr. Jeong can't compete.

736
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:40,289
We'll put in a supply order

737
00:41:41,749 --> 00:41:44,043
and cut off
Mr. Jeong's entire supply.

738
00:41:46,129 --> 00:41:47,338
Whose idea was this?

739
00:41:48,965 --> 00:41:50,341
It was Mr. Gong's.

740
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:57,223
Mr. Gong.

741
00:41:58,391 --> 00:41:59,976
Why a multi-brand shoe store?

742
00:42:04,731 --> 00:42:06,983
With clothing or accessories

743
00:42:07,066 --> 00:42:10,862
we also have to worry about hangers,
displays, props, and more.

744
00:42:10,945 --> 00:42:13,239
The downside to shoes is
that the boxes are bulky.

745
00:42:13,322 --> 00:42:16,534
But they're easy to manage
and require less preparation.

746
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:18,619
There's also less inventory per store

747
00:42:18,703 --> 00:42:20,163
and, after each season

748
00:42:20,246 --> 00:42:22,665
we can send leftovers to outlets,
which is an advantage.

749
00:42:23,833 --> 00:42:25,960
I believe it's a good project.

750
00:42:26,627 --> 00:42:28,463
Are you almost done
prepping the Laknes launch?

751
00:42:29,255 --> 00:42:30,256
Ms. Park.

752
00:42:31,424 --> 00:42:33,468
I came up with this project

753
00:42:34,052 --> 00:42:36,095
but it doesn't mean
only I can take it on.

754
00:42:36,679 --> 00:42:39,640
Even if you give it to another team,
I'll do my best to help out.

755
00:42:39,932 --> 00:42:40,933
Just answer the question.

756
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:43,811
Yes.

757
00:42:44,395 --> 00:42:46,147
Construction of the store's interior
is complete.

758
00:42:46,689 --> 00:42:48,024
We've also recruited managers.

759
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:50,234
So can you take this on?

760
00:42:50,943 --> 00:42:52,111
Yes, I can.

761
00:42:53,112 --> 00:42:54,572
- Mr. Jang.
- Yes, ma'am.

762
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:56,115
Schedule a meeting
with the Finance Team.

763
00:42:56,532 --> 00:42:59,452
- Mr. Gong, resubmit your proposal.
- Yes, ma'am.

764
00:42:59,786 --> 00:43:02,038
- And get ready for a trip to Mantua.
- Okay.

765
00:43:03,206 --> 00:43:04,207
Goodbye, ma'am.

766
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,255
Eun-tae.

767
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:13,841
You should pace yourself.

768
00:43:14,175 --> 00:43:16,094
At this rate,
you'll leave the rest of us behind.

769
00:43:16,177 --> 00:43:18,763
He's right. If you're going to do
the multi-brand shoe store

770
00:43:18,846 --> 00:43:21,015
you should give us
some of your other brands.

771
00:43:22,100 --> 00:43:24,227
Okay, I'll discuss it with Mr. Jang.

772
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:27,647
Yes, talk it over
and help Mr. Kim out.

773
00:43:28,523 --> 00:43:29,524
What?

774
00:43:29,899 --> 00:43:32,193
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Sorry?

775
00:43:32,276 --> 00:43:34,570
Who are you to tell him
to help me out?

776
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:37,907
Why would I take anything
from a junior colleague?

777
00:43:37,990 --> 00:43:39,075
I mean...

778
00:43:39,575 --> 00:43:42,203
Weren't you planning on
taking some of his brands?

779
00:43:42,286 --> 00:43:43,663
Why are you pretending?

780
00:43:44,205 --> 00:43:45,289
Look at this bastard.

781
00:43:45,957 --> 00:43:47,166
Then what about you?

782
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:49,127
Are you whining
because you couldn't even get scraps?

783
00:43:49,210 --> 00:43:50,545
"Whining"?

784
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:52,088
Are you serious?

785
00:43:52,380 --> 00:43:55,842
You're the one
snooping around a junior's team

786
00:43:55,925 --> 00:43:57,343
looking for scraps to take.

787
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:59,971
Has this bastard lost his mind?
Do you want to fight?

788
00:44:00,054 --> 00:44:02,181
Don't call me a bastard.
We're both team leaders.

789
00:44:02,265 --> 00:44:03,683
How dare you call me that?

790
00:44:03,766 --> 00:44:04,976
What are you, an associate director?

791
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:06,060
Hey!

792
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:17,280
What a great example you're setting
as team leaders.

793
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:21,075
Why don't you get back to work
instead of fighting?

794
00:44:21,325 --> 00:44:22,785
Cut the nonsense.

795
00:44:47,393 --> 00:44:53,232
<i>At a company, one person's decision
inevitably affects others.</i>

796
00:44:55,943 --> 00:44:59,655
<i>Everyone here is
both a cause and an effect</i>

797
00:45:00,114 --> 00:45:01,115
<i>of one another.</i>

798
00:45:07,914 --> 00:45:12,835
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

799
00:45:40,696 --> 00:45:43,824
2,034,320 WON SENT TO LEE JI-HYE
FROM HONGSUNG INTERNATIONAL

800
00:45:57,797 --> 00:45:58,965
Hello.

801
00:45:59,048 --> 00:46:00,091
Yes, hello.

802
00:46:00,383 --> 00:46:02,593
- How much is this?
- It's 32,000 won.

803
00:46:02,677 --> 00:46:04,011
Could you give me a discount?

804
00:46:04,095 --> 00:46:05,846
Hi, ladies.
Can I help you find something?

805
00:46:05,930 --> 00:46:06,931
- This is so pretty.
- This?

806
00:46:07,014 --> 00:46:08,099
If you like it...

807
00:46:16,023 --> 00:46:18,276
Excuse me, do you have that brown one
in another color?

808
00:46:18,985 --> 00:46:19,986
That's the last one we have.

809
00:46:20,987 --> 00:46:22,863
- How much is this?
- It's 60,000 won.

810
00:46:23,447 --> 00:46:24,782
All right, thank you.

811
00:46:30,121 --> 00:46:31,747
- Hello.
- Welcome.

812
00:46:31,831 --> 00:46:32,957
May I try this on?

813
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:35,209
Thank you.

814
00:46:41,924 --> 00:46:43,009
Thank you.

815
00:46:43,509 --> 00:46:45,136
It looks great on you.

816
00:46:45,219 --> 00:46:46,387
- Do you think so?
- Yeah.

817
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:53,602
- That one doesn't look good.
- Right?

818
00:46:56,814 --> 00:46:58,482
That one's so pretty on you.

819
00:46:58,566 --> 00:46:59,734
You should get it.

820
00:47:00,151 --> 00:47:01,235
Thank you.

821
00:47:01,319 --> 00:47:04,322
She said that when we first met.

822
00:47:04,405 --> 00:47:06,699
"Get me baseline margins
for the brands we're in charge of.

823
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:08,868
Customer prices,
customer service manuals..."

824
00:47:09,201 --> 00:47:11,662
You have no idea, right?
But that's not all.

825
00:47:11,746 --> 00:47:14,165
Credit memo logs,
invoice checklists...

826
00:47:14,248 --> 00:47:16,500
She asked me to prepare all of that.

827
00:47:16,584 --> 00:47:18,627
But do you know what's really crazy?

828
00:47:18,711 --> 00:47:20,504
I memorized it all in one shot.

829
00:47:20,588 --> 00:47:23,132
Isn't it?
You know I'm bad at memorization.

830
00:47:23,215 --> 00:47:25,259
Remember when I ran into my ex
on the street

831
00:47:25,343 --> 00:47:27,595
and stuttered like crazy
because I forgot his name?

832
00:47:28,387 --> 00:47:29,972
I don't know. I still don't remember.

833
00:47:30,056 --> 00:47:32,266
But I memorized all of that
in one shot.

834
00:47:32,350 --> 00:47:33,601
Isn't that amazing?

835
00:47:34,518 --> 00:47:36,937
But you can't just memorize
the words.

836
00:47:37,021 --> 00:47:39,648
There's a logical sequence
based on the workflow.

837
00:47:39,732 --> 00:47:41,484
That's how I memorized it.

838
00:47:41,567 --> 00:47:44,028
Can you imagine how nervous I was?

839
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:47,031
That assistant manager has
such a strong aura.

840
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:49,575
She looks at you
like she's studying you.

841
00:47:50,618 --> 00:47:53,662
Like a customs officer
looking you over.

842
00:47:53,746 --> 00:47:55,623
So imagine how hard I worked.

843
00:47:55,706 --> 00:47:57,375
I even lost my appetite.

844
00:47:57,458 --> 00:48:00,169
So when I brought her the file,
do you know what she said...

845
00:48:01,087 --> 00:48:02,588
Yes, what is it?

846
00:48:03,422 --> 00:48:04,965
Your boyfriend came?

847
00:48:05,049 --> 00:48:06,884
Okay, let's talk later.

848
00:48:06,967 --> 00:48:08,010
Bye.

849
00:48:13,682 --> 00:48:15,810
But this is the highlight.

850
00:48:16,977 --> 00:48:19,021
She said I did a great job.

851
00:48:22,942 --> 00:48:24,068
Darn it.

852
00:48:28,864 --> 00:48:30,324
Whatever, I did great.

853
00:51:04,270 --> 00:51:06,272
Subtitles by Eunice Kim

